```

## Manual Test

1. Install the unpacked extension, install the userscript in Tampermonkey, or paste it into a DevTools Snippet.
2. Open a GitHub PR files page.
3. Make sure the file explorer/sidebar is visible.
4. Click the locate icon in a file header.
5. Confirm the matching file tree item scrolls into view and flashes.
6. Click the terminal icon and configure your local repo root when prompted.
7. Confirm a command like `cursor -g "/path/to/repo/file.ts:123"` is copied.
8. Scroll down and confirm the back-to-top button appears.
9. Click it to jump to the top of the PR files area.
10. Shift-click it to jump to the absolute page top.

## Editor Command Settings

The terminal icon stores lightweight settings in browser `localStorage`:

```text
prFileExplorer.editor
prFileExplorer.repoRoot
```

Default editor is `cursor`. Option-click the terminal icon to reconfigure and use `code` instead.

